    "check": "Twelve names and figures read from the page image (BNL 21 May 1964, p. 7); the paper prints 'W. M. Loughlin' for Wilfred M'Laughlin (Irish News, 26 May 1964, p. 2: 'Wilfred McLaughlin'), and the Irish News gives Dr. Hamill 1,101 where the News-Letter prints 1,105 (kept). The two defeated Unionists (14 candidates for 12 seats) are not named in either report.",
    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0005119/19640521/149/0007"
  },
  "note": "Urban district election, 20 May 1964; whole council of twelve elected at large (Belfast News-Letter, 21 May 1964, p. 7). The report lists the twelve elected only; the unsuccessful candidates were not printed, so the poll cannot be completed here. Dr. Hamill topped the poll and Mr. Clements returned after nine years. Losers not printed: re-checked on the page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 21 May 1964, p. 7 (13 Nov 2026); a search of the British Newspaper Archive for 15 May to 6 June 1964 found no report naming the two defeated candidates.",
  "losersNotPrinted": true,
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of Belfast News-Letter, 21 May 1964, p. 7 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the paper prints 'W. M. Loughlin' (kept in Name_As_Printed), a misprint for the sitting member Wilfred M'Laughlin (Irish News, 26 May 1964, p. 2, and his other returns), so he is recorded as W. M'Laughlin."
